  "interpretation": [
    "Each row is paired with no injection by conversation (exact McNemar; Holm within the harmful-turn modes and within the turn-1 modes). The interval is Newcombe's hybrid score interval for a difference of paired proportions (method 10).",
    "Text-only modes steer the user text (and, at turn 1, the reply) but not the chat-template tokens after the request, where refusal is read out; the full modes steer those too, as single-turn steering does."
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Each condition is a single greedy run of the 8B model; behaviours are paired across conditions, so differences between conditions are compared behaviour by behaviour."
  ],
